{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b1f7c2a4-9d3e-4a21-8c5f-cards-api-0001",
    "name": "Cards API",
    "description": "setup_dev → Token → Catalog/Wallet → Upload → Transactions/Review.\n\nProtected requests inherit Bearer {{access_token}}. Run `python manage.py setup_dev` once to seed data and create user1 with a wallet card.\n\nValid rewards categories: `dining` | `groceries` | `travel` | `gas` | `entertainment` | `shopping` | `other`",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      { "key": "token", "value": "{{access_token}}", "type": "string" }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8000", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "username", "value": "user1", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "password", "value": "user1Password", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "access_token", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "refresh_token", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "user_card_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "upload_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "upload_filename", "value": "Chase_MAY_Transactions.csv", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "card_product_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "merchant_key", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "category", "value": "groceries", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Register",
      "request": {
        "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\",\n  \"password2\": \"{{password}}\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/register/",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "register", ""]
        },
        "description": "Optional if you already ran setup_dev. Expect 201, or 400 if user1 already exists."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Get Token (login)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  const res = pm.response.json();",
              "  if (res.access)  pm.collectionVariables.set('access_token', res.access);",
              "  if (res.refresh) pm.collectionVariables.set('refresh_token', res.refresh);",
              "  console.log('Saved access + refresh tokens to collection variables.');",
              "} else {",
              "  console.log('Token request failed:', pm.response.code, pm.response.text());",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/token/",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "token", ""]
        },
        "description": "Public. Returns access + refresh. Tests script auto-saves both. Auth on this request must be No Auth."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Catalog Cards (protected)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  const res = pm.response.json();",
              "  if (res.cards && res.cards.length > 0) {",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('card_product_id', String(res.cards[0].id));",
              "    console.log('Saved card_product_id:', res.cards[0].id);",
              "  }",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/cards/",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "cards", ""]
        },
        "description": "Protected. Lists active catalog products you can add to your wallet / use for Day 5 recommendations. Saves first id to {{card_product_id}}."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Wallet — List (protected)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  const res = pm.response.json();",
              "  if (res.cards && res.cards.length > 0) {",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('user_card_id', String(res.cards[0].id));",
              "    console.log('Saved user_card_id:', res.cards[0].id);",
              "  }",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/wallet/",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "wallet", ""]
        },
        "description": "Protected. Cards you own. Each `id` is the user_card_id for upload. Tests script saves the first id."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Wallet — Add catalog (protected)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
              "  const res = pm.response.json();",
              "  if (res.id) pm.collectionVariables.set('user_card_id', String(res.id));",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"card_product_id\": {{card_product_id}}\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/wallet/",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "wallet", ""]
        },
        "description": "Protected. Add from catalog by id. 201 on success; 400 if already in wallet, unknown, or inactive. Saves {{user_card_id}}."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "5b. Wallet — Add custom (protected)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
              "  const res = pm.response.json();",
              "  if (res.id) pm.collectionVariables.set('user_card_id', String(res.id));",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Campus Visa\",\n  \"issuer\": \"Local CU\",\n  \"network\": \"Visa\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/wallet/",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "wallet", ""]
        },
        "description": "Protected. Free-text card (name + issuer + network required). Creates is_catalog=false product with zero rewards, or attaches an existing name+issuer match (including catalog). 400 on duplicate in your wallet."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "6. Wallet — Delete (protected)",
      "request": {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/wallet/{{user_card_id}}/",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "wallet", "{{user_card_id}}", ""]
        },
        "description": "Protected. HARD delete wallet row + its Transactions. If the product was custom and unused, the Card_Products row is removed too. Catalog products are kept."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "7. Upload Transactions (protected)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.response.code === 201 || pm.response.code === 200 || pm.response.code === 207) {",
              "  const res = pm.response.json();",
              "  if (res.upload_id) {",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('upload_id', String(res.upload_id));",
              "  } else if (res.results && res.results.length) {",
              "    const firstOk = res.results.find(r => r.ok && r.upload_id) || res.results[0];",
              "    if (firstOk && firstOk.upload_id) pm.collectionVariables.set('upload_id', String(firstOk.upload_id));",
              "  }",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "formdata",
          "formdata": [
            {
              "key": "file",
              "type": "file",
              "src": [],
              "description": "Select one or more CSVs under backend/data/sample_uploads/. In Postman: add another `file` row (same key) for each extra statement, or multi-select if your client supports it."
            },
            {
              "key": "file",
              "type": "file",
              "src": [],
              "disabled": true,
              "description": "Optional second statement — enable and pick another CSV to upload both in one request."
            },
            {
              "key": "user_card_id",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "{{user_card_id}}",
              "description": "Wallet entry id from GET /api/wallet/ (shared across all files in this request)"
            }
          ]
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/upload/",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "upload", ""]
        },
        "description": "Protected. form-data: one or more `file` fields + `user_card_id`.\n\n- **One file** → same shape as before (`upload_id`, `summary`, …). 201 create / 200 refresh.\n- **Multiple files** → `{ count, succeeded, failed, results[] }` with per-file `ok` / `detail`. 201 all-new, 200 all-refresh, 207 mixed, 400 all failed.\n\nSame bytes + same card refreshes. Same bytes + different card → 409 — use reassign."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "7b. List Uploads (protected)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.response.code !== 200) { return; }",
              "const res = pm.response.json();",
              "const uploads = res.uploads || [];",
              "uploads.forEach(u => console.log(`upload_id=${u.upload_id}  file=${u.filename}  card=${u.card_name}`));",
              "const want = (pm.collectionVariables.get('upload_filename') || '').trim();",
              "let chosen = null;",
              "if (want) {",
              "  chosen = uploads.find(u => u.filename === want)",
              "    || uploads.find(u => (u.filename || '').includes(want));",
              "}",
              "if (!chosen && uploads.length === 1) { chosen = uploads[0]; }",
              "if (chosen) {",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('upload_id', String(chosen.upload_id));",
              "  console.log('Selected upload_id', chosen.upload_id, 'for', chosen.filename);",
              "} else {",
              "  console.log('No auto-select. Set collection var upload_filename to a listed file, or paste upload_id into 7c/7d.');",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/uploads/",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "uploads", ""]
        },
        "description": "Protected. **This is how you pick which statement to reassign or delete** — no re-upload needed.\n\nResponse lists every import: `upload_id`, `filename`, `user_card_id`, `card_name`, `transaction_count`.\n\nTests script:\n- Logs all uploads to the console\n- If collection var `upload_filename` matches a listed file, saves that `upload_id` for 7c/7d\n- If only one upload exists, selects it\n- Otherwise leave `upload_id` blank and paste the id you want into 7c or 7d"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "7c. Reassign Upload Card (protected)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"user_card_id\": {{user_card_id}}\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/uploads/{{upload_id}}/reassign/",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "uploads", "{{upload_id}}", "reassign", ""]
        },
        "description": "Protected. Moves every transaction on **this upload_id** to another wallet card.\n\n1. Run 7b List Uploads (set `upload_filename` to e.g. Chase_MAY_Transactions.csv)\n2. Set `user_card_id` to the **destination** wallet card\n3. Send — do **not** re-upload the CSV first"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "7d. Delete Upload (protected)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.response.code === 204) {",
              "  console.log('Deleted upload_id', pm.collectionVariables.get('upload_id'));",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('upload_id', '');",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/uploads/{{upload_id}}/",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "uploads", "{{upload_id}}", ""]
        },
        "description": "Protected. Hard-deletes the statement import for **this upload_id** and cascades its transactions.\n\n1. Run 7b List Uploads to set `upload_id` (or paste one)\n2. Send — expect **204 No Content**\n3. Re-run 7b / 8 / 11 to confirm the statement and its spend are gone\n\nForeign or unknown ids → 404."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "8. List Transactions (protected)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/transactions/",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "transactions", ""]
        },
        "description": "Protected. Includes `upload_id` + `filename` so you can see which statement a row belongs to before reassigning."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "9. Review Queue (protected)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  const res = pm.response.json();",
              "  if (res.merchants && res.merchants.length > 0) {",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('merchant_key', res.merchants[0].merchant_key);",
              "    console.log('Saved top merchant_key:', res.merchants[0].merchant_key);",
              "  } else {",
              "    console.log('Review queue empty — nothing to label.');",
              "  }",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/review/",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "review", ""]
        },
        "description": "Protected. Unresolved merchants for your spend."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "10. Review Answer (protected)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"merchant_key\": \"{{merchant_key}}\",\n  \"category\": \"{{category}}\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/review/answer/",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "review", "answer", ""]
        },
        "description": "Protected. Label a merchant; backfills your transactions."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "11. Spend Summary (protected)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/summary/",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "summary", ""]
        },
        "description": "Protected. All-time spend totals by rewards category across all wallet cards.\n\nResponse fields:\n- by_category: all 7 buckets (dining, groceries, travel, gas, entertainment, shopping, other) as net spend strings\n- annualized: projected annual spend per category (by_category × 12 / months_covered)\n- total_spend: sum of all by_category values\n- transaction_count: total rows across all uploads\n- unresolved_count / unresolved_amount: rows still needing review\n- categorized_pct: count-based coverage, 1 decimal place\n- period: earliest/latest transaction date, days_span (display only) + months_covered\n\nmonths_covered counts distinct calendar months holding a transaction. Statements arrive with gaps, so an April statement plus a July one is 2 months of evidence across 103 calendar days — annualizing on days_span would read the empty gap as months of zero spending.\n\nAll money values are 2-decimal strings. Run Upload (step 7) first for non-zero totals. Run Review Answer (step 10) to improve categorized_pct."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "12. Recommendations (protected)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const MONEY = /^-?\\d+\\.\\d{2}$/;",
              "const STATUSES = ['met', 'not_met', 'insufficient_data', 'no_bonus'];",
              "const FIELDS = ['rank', 'card_id', 'card_name', 'issuer', 'reward_currency',",
              "  'headline', 'spending_score', 'annual_fee', 'signup_bonus_score',",
              "  'signup_bonus_status', 'signup_bonus_note', 'total_score',",
              "  'ongoing_annual_value', 'break_even_annual_spend', 'explanation'];",
              "",
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const res = pm.response.json();",
              "",
              "pm.test('envelope has confidence + value_basis + recommendations', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(res).to.have.property('confidence');",
              "  pm.expect(res).to.have.property('confidence_note');",
              "  pm.expect(res).to.have.property('value_basis');",
              "  pm.expect(res.recommendations).to.be.an('array');",
              "});",
              "",
              "const recs = res.recommendations || [];",
              "pm.test('at most 5 recommendations', () => pm.expect(recs.length).to.be.at.most(5));",
              "",
              "recs.forEach((c, i) => {",
              "  const label = '#' + (i + 1) + ' ' + c.card_name;",
              "  pm.test(label + ': contract fields present', () => {",
              "    FIELDS.forEach(f => pm.expect(c).to.have.property(f));",
              "  });",
              "  pm.test(label + ': money fields are 2-decimal strings', () => {",
              "    ['spending_score', 'annual_fee', 'signup_bonus_score', 'total_score', 'ongoing_annual_value']",
              "      .forEach(f => pm.expect(c[f]).to.match(MONEY));",
              "  });",
              "  pm.test(label + ': total = spend - fee + bonus', () => {",
              "    const expected = Number(c.spending_score) - Number(c.annual_fee) + Number(c.signup_bonus_score);",
              "    // each field is rounded on its own, so allow one cent of drift",
              "    pm.expect(Math.abs(Number(c.total_score) - expected)).to.be.at.most(0.011);",
              "  });",
              "  pm.test(label + ': ongoing value excludes the bonus', () => {",
              "    const expected = Number(c.spending_score) - Number(c.annual_fee);",
              "    pm.expect(Math.abs(Number(c.ongoing_annual_value) - expected)).to.be.at.most(0.011);",
              "  });",
              "  pm.test(label + ': break-even set only when a fee needs covering', () => {",
              "    const needed = Number(c.annual_fee) > 0 && Number(c.spending_score) > 0;",
              "    pm.expect(c.break_even_annual_spend !== null).to.eql(needed);",
              "  });",
              "  pm.test(label + ': signup_bonus_status is valid', () => {",
              "    pm.expect(STATUSES).to.include(c.signup_bonus_status);",
              "    pm.expect(Number(c.signup_bonus_score) > 0).to.eql(c.signup_bonus_status === 'met');",
              "  });",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('competition ranks (ties share a rank)', () => {",
              "  recs.forEach((c, i) => {",
              "    pm.expect(c.rank).to.be.at.most(i + 1);",
              "    if (i > 0) pm.expect(c.rank).to.be.at.least(recs[i - 1].rank);",
              "    // rank_note is omitted entirely unless this card ties",
              "    if ('rank_note' in c) pm.expect(c.rank_note).to.include('Tied with');",
              "  });",
              "});",
              "",
              "console.log('confidence:', res.confidence, res.confidence_note);",
              "console.log('basis:', JSON.stringify(res.value_basis));",
              "recs.forEach(c => console.log('#' + c.rank + ' ' + c.card_name + ' — ' + c.headline));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/recommendations/",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "recommendations", ""]
        },
        "description": "Protected. Top ≤5 catalog cards scored against this user's spend summary.\n\nEvery money field is estimated US dollars per year — see `value_basis` in the response.\n\nResponse fields:\n- confidence / confidence_note: reliability of the underlying summary\n- value_basis: currency, months_of_data, point_value_cents\n- recommendations[]: rank, card_id, card_name, issuer, reward_currency, headline, spending_score, annual_fee, signup_bonus_score/status/note, total_score, ongoing_annual_value, break_even_annual_spend, explanation[]\n- rank_note is **omitted** unless the card ties with another\n\nFormulas:\n- spending uses annualized spend × effective rate%; negatives floored to 0\n- annualized = by_category × 12 / months_covered (months holding transactions, not calendar span)\n- points/miles convert at value_basis.point_value_cents before entering any dollar figure\n- signup bonus uses actual by_category; insufficient_data until months_covered reaches the card's window\n- total_score = spending_score − annual_fee + signup_bonus_score (first year)\n- ongoing_annual_value = spending_score − annual_fee (every year after)\n- break_even_annual_spend: spend at this user's mix that would cover the fee; null when there is no fee\n- residual ties share Olympic rank (e.g. 1,1,3) with rank_note\n\nNegative totals are meaningful: the annual fee costs more than the card returns.\n\nZero transactions → recommendations: [] (still 200, often confidence=low). Ranking needs statement spend. Run Upload + Summary first for meaningful ranks. Clear review queue to raise confidence."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "13. Refresh Token",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  const res = pm.response.json();",
              "  if (res.access) pm.collectionVariables.set('access_token', res.access);",
              "  console.log('Refreshed access token.');",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"refresh\": \"{{refresh_token}}\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/token/refresh/",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "token", "refresh", ""]
        },
        "description": "Public. Exchanges refresh for a new access token (auto-saved)."
      }
    }
  ]
}
